// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/ai_assist.t27 -- the boundary around model-generated text
; One subject: what an external language model may say to a TurboBaby customer, what may be put
; in front of it, and what is sent when it says nothing. src/ai.rs calls a paid model and hands
; back an Option; six call sites spend that Option. This file owns the edges of that Option and
; nothing inside it. It holds no prompt text, no fleet row, no rate, no status and no key.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). Nothing in this corpus constrained the one component that writes
; sentences nobody reviewed -- past tense, and the tense is the claim. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21
; against the finished 43-file corpus: 3 of the other 42 files now name turbobaby/ai-assist, and
; every one of the three DEFERS to this file rather than constraining the boundary itself.
; turbobaby/bot-surface co-declares the escape rule and names this file as the co-declarer;
; turbobaby/promo-broadcast hands it the draft copy check; turbobaby/rate-limit is consumed here
; as a boolean. So the absence has become an ownership: the constraint exists now, it is this
; file, and no second contract states it. A reader who greps ai-assist and gets 3 has found the
; edges, not a rival owner. Six call sites spend ask_grok (src/ai.rs:185-222): four
; entertainment sites (src/bot/commands.rs:355 and :382, src/bot/callbacks.rs:259 and :297), one
; free-text site that answers whatever a customer types, in a private chat or a public group
; (src/bot/handlers.rs:75), and one owner-draft site (src/promo.rs:456). FIVE of those six reach
; a customer with no human in between. On the way IN the boundary is bounded three times --
; 2000 characters of prompt (src/ai.rs:147), 100 of persona (src/ai.rs:148), 1500 at the
; free-text door (src/bot/handlers.rs:39). On the way OUT it is bounded ZERO times on those five
; sites: src/util.rs:8-15 truncate_string is called at src/ai.rs:154, src/ai.rs:202 and
; src/bot/handlers.rs:39 and at no site on a returned answer, and the only content check that
; exists anywhere -- src/trios/promo.rs:277-299 usable_copy -- serves the sixth site, the one a
; customer cannot see without an owner pressing publish. The asymmetry is the reason for this
; file: the shop bounds what it pays for and does not bound what it says.
; One more measured number belongs in the same paragraph, because it is the only place on this
; boundary where a customer gets nothing: of the five sites a limiter guards, four answer a
; refused turn with a literal and ONE answers with silence -- src/bot/handlers.rs:58-61 logs a
; warning and returns Ok(()) with no send.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Three corrections and one timing note, each measured and each kept
; as a constant so it is checkable rather than asserted. The three are (1), (3) and (4); (2) is
; the brief being right about an edge that had not landed yet, recorded because the grep behind
; it has since changed its answer.
; (1) "Two bot commands" undercounts by four. /joke and /fact are two of SIX ask_grok call
; sites, and the two the brief omits are the interesting ones: the two repeat buttons
; (src/bot/callbacks.rs:259 and :297) reach the same customer with no command typed, and the
; free-text site (src/bot/handlers.rs:75) is the only one that puts a customer's own words and
; a customer's own display name into a paid prompt. A contract built on the brief's two would
; have left the datum-carrying path outside the boundary it claims to draw.
; (2) The reuse edge turbobaby/bot-surface was absent when this file began and is real now. At
; the first measurement grep -rn "bot-surface" specs/ returned zero and the twenty pub const ID
; lines held no such value; turbobaby/bot-surface landed during the same wave and
; declares that ID as its own ID constant -- VERIFIED 2026-09-21, the declaration is there and
; still carries that literal. The edge below is therefore a measured fact and not a forward
; declaration, and the earlier zero is kept rather than deleted: a reader who repeats the grep
; today gets a different answer than the survey did, and the difference is the corpus growing
; under the measurement rather than either count being wrong. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21: the same
; grep now returns 9 of the 43 files. THAT FIGURE READ 10 UNTIL THE CORPUS AUDIT OF THE SAME DATE
; RE-RAN IT, and the correction is kept in view rather than quietly applied, because a count that
; is one too high is the same defect as an absence that is stale: both are trusted unread. The
; audit ran the file form of the grep over the finished manifest and got nine paths, this file
; among them; no reading of the command -- lines, matches or paths -- yields ten, so the 10 was
; not a different scope but a wrong number. The scope is pinned beside the count below so the
; next reader does not have to guess which of the three readings was meant.
; The citation that used to stand here was a LINE NUMBER
; into that file, and it had drifted twice by the time it was re-read, which is why the ID and
; the declaration name are what is cited now.
; (3) The brief offers the prompt question as a fork -- shop facts, or nothing -- and the
; measured answer is BOTH, split by path. The entertainment prompts carry nothing the shop
; knows: a fixed base string, one of 23 styles (src/ai.rs:7-31) or one of 22 topics
; (src/ai.rs:33-56), and a literal persona. The draft prompt carries a price read out of the
; database (src/promo.rs:506-539, formatted at :507). So the guarantee had to be written per
; kind, and the one that matters is the conjunction: no path that reaches a customer unreviewed
; carries a shop fact into a prompt.
; (4) The survey cites src/locales.rs:26 and :31 for the two fallback strings. :31 is right and
; :26 is not: :26 declares joke_prompt, which is prompt input, and the fallback beside it is
; :27 joke_fail_fallback. The pair is :27 and :31. The correction matters because :26 is the
; field that goes INTO the model and :27 is the field that replaces it, and a contract that
; confused them would have pinned the failure path to the prompt.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It states no price, no rate, no availability count, no status and
; no term: those belong to the four named owners below, and this file consumes their decisions
; as booleans and their identities as strings. It carries no prompt text and no system-prompt
; wording -- a prompt copied into a spec is a second prompt to maintain, and the one in
; src/ai.rs:155-159 is not this file's to freeze. It pins no provider and no model name as a
; guarantee: src/ai.rs:226 and :262 name four model strings and src/ai.rs:236 and :264-265 name
; three endpoints, and any of up to seven attempts may supply the answer, so naming one here
; would promise an identity the code does not keep. It makes no claim about the quality,
; accuracy, language or usefulness of what comes back -- nothing in this repository reads a
; reply and judges it on any of those axes, and a spec that claimed otherwise would be the
; corpus's only unmeasured promise. It quotes no shipped Cyrillic string: the two fallbacks, the
; language instruction and the draft copy are cited by field name, and the too-fast refusal --
; which is not a field but a literal written in place -- by path alone (L3). It restates nothing
; owned by the three contracts that landed beside it: the draft-to-send boundary, the owner
; press that crosses it and the length-and-refusal check on a
; drafted post are turbobaby/promo-broadcast's, measured there as send_is_authorized and
; copy_is_usable, and this file names that ID rather than copying either function or its two
; character figures; the escape rule, its three characters and its call-site counts are
; turbobaby/bot-surface's, and what is kept here is one boolean over this file's own six sites
; and no list of them; whether a caller is inside its window is turbobaby/rate-limit's, arriving
; here as a boolean argument, and no window, cooldown or key derivation appears below.
; It carries no renter, handle, phone, key code, plate, debt, purchase price or
; personal note (D14) -- and pointedly not the one customer datum the code does put in a prompt,
; the Telegram display name at src/bot/handlers.rs:63-73.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-ai-assist;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/ai-assist";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby model-output boundary";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const DECISIONS : [2]str = ["D13", "D14"];
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";

; --- Ownership edges -------------------------------------------------------------------------
